{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nsys.stderr = sys.stdout\n\ndef make_coeffs(n, mod):\n    c = [0] * (n + 1)\n    c[n] = 1\n    for k in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        c[k] = (c[k + 1] * (k + 1)) % mod\n        if c[k] == 0:\n            break\n    return c\n\ndef build_flat(n, mod):\n    tables = [[1]]\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        old = tables[i]\n        old_width = i + 1\n        old_rows = len(old) // old_width\n        new_width = old_width + 1\n        new_rows = old_rows + old_width\n        new = [0] * (new_rows * new_width)\n        for j in range(old_rows):\n            for col in range(old_width):\n                value = old[j * old_width + col]\n                for off in range(old_width):\n                    idx = (j + off) * new_width + col\n                    new[idx] = (new[idx] + value) % mod\n                idx = (j + old_width) * new_width + old_width\n                new[idx] = (new[idx] + value) % mod\n        tables.append(new)\n    return tables\n\ndef contribution(flat, width, mod, coeff):\n    R = len(flat) // width\n    pref = [0] * (R * width)\n    for r in range(R):\n        acc = 0\n        for c in range(width - 1, -1, -1):\n            acc = (acc + flat[r * width + c]) % mod\n            pref[r * width + c] = acc\n    for r in range(1, R):\n        base = r * width\n        prevbase = (r - 1) * width\n        for c in range(width):\n            pref[base + c] = (pref[base + c] + pref[prevbase + c]) % mod\n    part = 0\n    for r in range(1, R):\n        base = r * width\n        prevbase = (r - 1) * width\n        for c in range(width - 1):\n            part = (part + flat[base + c] * pref[prevbase + c + 1]) % mod\n    return (part * coeff) % mod\n\ndef solve(n, mod):\n    coeffs = make_coeffs(n, mod)\n    tables = build_flat(n, mod)\n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        width = i + 1\n        ans = (ans + contribution(tables[i], width, mod, coeffs[i + 1])) % mod\n    return ans\n\ndef main():\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    print(solve(n, m))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nvector<ll> make_coeffs(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<ll> c(n + 1, 0);\n    c[n] = 1;\n    for (int k = n - 1; k >= 0; --k) {\n        c[k] = (c[k + 1] * (k + 1)) % mod;\n        if (c[k] == 0) break;\n    }\n    return c;\n}\n\nvector<vector<ll>> build_flat(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<vector<ll>> tables;\n    tables.push_back({1}); // width = 1\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {\n        vector<ll>& old = tables[i];\n        int old_width = i + 1;\n        int old_rows = old.size() / old_width;\n        int new_width = old_width + 1;\n        int new_rows = old_rows + old_width;\n        vector<ll> new_table(new_rows * new_width, 0);\n        for (int j = 0; j < old_rows; ++j) {\n            for (int col = 0; col < old_width; ++col) {\n                ll value = old[j * old_width + col];\n                for (int off = 0; off < old_width; ++off) {\n                    int idx = (j + off) * new_width + col;\n                    new_table[idx] = (new_table[idx] + value) % mod;\n                }\n                int idx = (j + old_width) * new_width + old_width;\n                new_table[idx] = (new_table[idx] + value) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n        tables.push_back(new_table);\n    }\n    return tables;\n}\n\nll contribution(const vector<ll>& flat, int width, ll mod, ll coeff) {\n    int R = flat.size() / width;\n    vector<ll> pref(R * width, 0);\n    for (int r = 0; r < R; ++r) {\n        ll acc = 0;\n        for (int c = width - 1; c >= 0; --c) {\n            acc = (acc + flat[r * width + c]) % mod;\n            pref[r * width + c] = acc;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int r = 1; r < R; ++r) {\n        int base = r * width;\n        int prevbase = (r - 1) * width;\n        for (int c = 0; c < width; ++c) {\n            pref[base + c] = (pref[base + c] + pref[prevbase + c]) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    ll part = 0;\n    for (int r = 1; r < R; ++r) {\n        int base = r * width;\n        int prevbase = (r - 1) * width;\n        for (int c = 0; c < width - 1; ++c) {\n            part = (part + flat[base + c] * pref[prevbase + c + 1]) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    return (part * coeff) % mod;\n}\n\nll solve(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<ll> coeffs = make_coeffs(n, mod);\n    vector<vector<ll>> tables = build_flat(n, mod);\n    ll ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; ++i) {\n        int width = i + 1;\n        ans = (ans + contribution(tables[i], width, mod, coeffs[i + 1])) % mod;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    ll m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    cout << solve(n, m) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00010978573118336499, -0.0009255892946384847, -1.1920858014491387e-05, -0.